            "<strong>Postvention</strong> is care after a suicide. The bereaved family carry grief, guilt, shame, anger and sometimes stigma from a community that still believes suicide is a sin or a curse; they need to be told plainly that the illness, not they, caused the death, to be helped with the practicalities, and to be followed up, because they are themselves at raised risk. When a <strong>patient dies by suicide</strong> on the ward or soon after discharge, the <strong>staff</strong> need support too: the nurse who did the last check carries it for years. A structured debrief within days, honest review of what could be learned without blame, time off where needed, supervision and, where there is an inquiry, support through it, are the responsibility of the manager. Silence and scapegoating drive nurses out of the profession and teach the rest to hide risk.",
